'''Yveltal''' (Japanese: '''イベルタル''' ''Yveltal'') is a major character in ''[[M17|Diancie and the Cocoon of Destruction]]''.

==In the movies==
[[File:Yveltal Dark Aura.png|thumb|left|250px|Activating {{a|Dark Aura}}]]
Hundreds of years prior to the {{pkmn|movie}}'s events, Yveltal almost destroyed all life in [[Allearth Forest]]. {{OBP|Xerneas|M17}} saved {{DL|Carbink servants|Dace}} and many other Pokémon from the destruction, and later reversed all of the damage that Yveltal inflicted. After these events, Yveltal turned into a giant cocoon and slumbered until the present day.

During that time, [[Argus Steel|Argus]] and [[Millis Steel]], [[Merilyn]], and [[Riot]] were fighting over who should catch {{an|Diancie}}. They eventually took their fighting to an underground pool where Yveltal slept in its cocoon form. The fighting eventually awakened Yveltal, and it immediately activated its {{a|Dark Aura}} and used {{m|Oblivion Wing}} to petrify large areas of the forest, as well as {{TRT}}, Merilyn, Riot, the Carbink servants (save for Dace), and the Steels, who tried to stop it with missiles from their ship. {{Ash}} and {{AP|Pikachu}} tried to battle Yveltal as well, but almost fell off a cliff, with Pikachu being petrified in the process. Diancie [[Mega Evolution|Mega Evolved]] and created a large diamond, which she used to protect Ash, {{an|Serena}}, {{an|Clemont}}, and {{an|Bonnie}} from another Oblivion Wing. Yveltal used Oblivion Wing once again to finish them off, but the attack was intercepted by Xerneas' Aurora Beam. Yveltal, still in its Dark Aura state, used Shadow Ball, which Xerneas intercepted with another Aurora Beam before using its Fairy Aura to successfully calm Yveltal. With nothing more to do, it flew away peacefully.

Yveltal was last seen flying through a mountainous area at night during the ending credits.

===Personality and characteristics===
Yveltal appears to be a very destructive Pokémon, destroying the [[Allearth Forest]] with its {{m|Oblivion Wing}}, particularly seeking to destroy those who disturbed its sleep in the form of a cocoon as payment for disturbing it. This is also seen when it destroyed all life in the Allearth Forest years prior to the events of the movie. However, Yveltal is not always openly destructive, as it left in peace once Xerneas calmed it with its Fairy Aura.

